<div class="entry-content single-content">
	
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Most small laundry room ideas assume you have a front-loading washer. They show countertops, cabinets and stacked machines, none of which work when your washer opens from the top.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A top-loader changes the rules: the lid needs open space above it, and anything you store on top of the machine has to move every time you do a load. This guide shows you how to plan around that, with a simple clearance guide and 15 small laundry room ideas that actually work with a top loading washer.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" width="1024" height="1024" src="https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/laundry-01-small-laundry.jpg" alt="Small laundry room ideas with a top loading washer: white top-loader and dryer under high wooden shelves with baskets and jars" class="wp-image-695" srcset="https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/laundry-01-small-laundry.jpg 1024w, https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/laundry-01-small-laundry-300x300.jpg 300w, https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/laundry-01-small-laundry-150x150.jpg 150w, https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/laundry-01-small-laundry-768x768.jpg 768w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>



<div class="wp-block-group dsh-summary has-background" style="border-radius:12px;border-left-color:#8FA689;border-left-width:5px;background-color:#EEF3EC;padding-top:20px;padding-right:24px;padding-bottom:20px;padding-left:24px"><div class="wp-block-group__inner-container is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-0d2d72cd wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Key Takeaways</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Quick answer:</strong> The best small laundry room ideas with a top loading washer keep the lid clear: hang shelves above the fully open lid plus a few inches, and use the gaps beside the machines, the walls and the door for storage.</li>


<li>Leave enough clearance so the washer lid can open fully under any shelf.</li>



<li>Use the gaps beside the machines, the walls and the space above for storage.</li>



<li>Keep detergent pods and chemicals out of children&#8217;s reach.</li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Time:</strong> 1–3 hours · <strong>Cost:</strong> $20–100 · <strong>Difficulty:</strong> Easy</p>
