ents__entry" href="#can-you-put-a-shelf-above-a-top-loading-washer">Can you put a shelf above a top loading washer?</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#how-high-should-a-shelf-be-above-a-top-loader">How high should a shelf be above a top loader?</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#can-you-put-a-countertop-over-a-toploading-washer">Can you put a countertop over a top-loading washer?</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#how-do-i-make-a-small-laundry-room-more-functional">How do I make a small laundry room more functional?</a></li></ul></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#final-thoughts">Final Thoughts</a></li></ul></div></nav>


<h2 class="wp-block-heading">The Top-Loader Rule: Keep the Space Above the Lid Clear</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">With a front-loader, the space above the machine is free real estate. With a top-loader, it&#8217;s a no-storage zone up to the height of the open lid. Put a shelf, cabinet or countertop too low and the lid won&#8217;t open fully, which makes loading and unloading a daily annoyance.</p>



